{{Quote|The Bith see the poetry in the mathematics of music; I see the poetry in the mathematics of money.|Djas Puhr|<ref name="The Kloo Horn Cantina Caper">{{StoryCite|story=The Kloo Horn Cantina Caper|book=From a Certain Point of View}}</ref>}}
'''Djas Puhr''' was a [[Gender|male]] [[Sakiyan]] [[bounty hunter]] active during the [[Imperial Era|Age of the Empire]]. He was an associate of the [[smuggler]] [[Han Solo]], and frequented [[Chalmun's Spaceport Cantina]] on the [[planet]] [[Tatooine]].

==Biography==
===Mysterious past===
{{Quote|Word of advice, kid&mdash;you are in over your head. Should choose your bounty jobs more carefully.''"<br />"''<nowiki />''E chu ta''.|Djas Puhr and Boba Fett|<ref name="Black, White & Red 3">[[Boba Fett — Black, White & Red 3|''Boba Fett — Black, White & Red'' 3]]</ref>}}
Few knew the past of Djas Puhr,<ref name="The Kloo Horn Cantina Caper" /> a [[Gender|male]] [[Sakiyan]]<ref name="SWFC" /> who left his [[homeworld]]. It was rumored that he was an ex-[[Slavery|slave]], who had climbed out of the slave pits of [[Hutt Clan|Hutt Cartel]] [[gangster]] [[Jabba Desilijic Tiure]]; whatever the reason, Puhr harbored a hatred towards the [[crime lord]], and refused to take [[Bounty|bounties]] from [[Jabba's criminal empire|his organization]].<ref name="The Kloo Horn Cantina Caper" />

Drinking at the [[Blood Oath Syndicate|Blood Oath]] [[spice]] den on [[Ord Radama]], Puhr noticed another [[bounty hunter|hunter]] enter the establishment: [[Boba Fett]]. Puhr advised young Fett, who had come for the bounty on the [[Kajain'sa'Nikto]] [[Corm Vargon]], that he was in over his head, suggesting he choose his targets more carefully. Fett coarsely replied ''e chu ta'',<ref name="Black, White & Red 3" /> a [[Huttese]] insult.<ref name="SYWtBaJ?">''[[The Empire Strikes Back: So You Want to Be a Jedi?]]''</ref>

Puhr was an associate of the [[smuggler]] [[Han Solo]] and his [[First Mate|first mate]] [[Chewbacca]]. Puhr and Solo had an agreement whereby Solo would deliver him [[gwayo bird]] [[egg]]s, a delicacy of Puhr's homeworld, along with his regular cargo of [[spice]] for Jabba.<ref name="The Kloo Horn Cantina Caper" /> During one of these shipments, Solo was forced to drop his spice cargo to avoid arrest by the [[Galactic Empire]], causing Jabba to place a 50,000-credit bounty on his head and throwing the standing of his agreement with Puhr into question.<ref name="Character Encyclopedia: New Edition">''[[Star Wars Character Encyclopedia, New Edition]]''</ref>

===Tatooine===
{{Quote|Let us wager on the nature of the universe. Who wins? The man with friends, or the man seeking profit at all costs?|Djas Puhr, on the confrontation between Han Solo and Greedo|<ref name="The Kloo Horn Cantina Caper" />}}
[[File:Muftak_drinking.jpg|250px|thumb|Myo, Muftak, Lirin Car'n, and Djas Puhr at their table in the cantina]]
In [[1 BBY]],<ref name="ANH Date">{{FilmDate|IV|1}}</ref> Puhr was present in the [[spaceport]] of [[Mos Eisley]] on the planet [[Tatooine]].<ref name="ANH">{{Film|IV}}</ref> He was known to frequent [[Chalmun's Spaceport Cantina]], where he considered himself a regular. The [[bounty hunter]] often sat at a table with [[Myo]], [[Muftak]], and [[Kabe]]—a cohort which he enjoyed, for all of its foibles.<ref name="The Kloo Horn Cantina Caper" />

Around this [[time]], he was hired by Myo to retrieve a valuable [[kloo horn]], which the [[Abyssin]] had [[Gambling|won]] in a card game from [[Lirin Car'n]] the night before before becoming intoxicated and losing it himself. Car'n, a member of the [[Figrin D'an and the Modal Nodes|Modal Nodes]] house [[band]] (and son of the horn's previous owner, the late, great [[Lirin D'avi]]), desperately needed [[Currency|money]] to pay off a debt to [[Rodian]] bounty hunter [[Greedo]]. With this in mind, Lirin Car'n also hired Puhr for the same task, promising to pay two hundred [[Galactic Credit Standard|credits]] to retrieve it.<ref name="The Kloo Horn Cantina Caper" />

The Sakiyan bounty hunter easily found the horn—which had been stolen by Muftak and Kabe and sold in order to pay their rent—and acquired it from [[the Scrapper]]. After a brief confrontation with [[Han Solo]] and [[Chewbacca]] (whom he warned about the bounty on their heads), he returned to his regular table. In the course of the heated conversation between his companions, it became clear that the group's various problems stemmed from the smuggler Solo's failure to deliver his cargo of narcotics to Muftak. Knowing that Greedo planned to collect on Solo's bounty that same [[Standard day|day]], Puhr made a wager on the smuggler's life, promising to "pay off" the group's various debts himself, should Solo live.<ref name="The Kloo Horn Cantina Caper" />

After his henchmen, [[Cornelius Evazan]] and [[Ponda Baba]], were incapacitated by a [[Obi-Wan Kenobi|third party]], Greedo's attempt failed, and he was killed by Solo.<ref name="ANH" /> Puhr, content with the outcome of the situation and the justice of the [[universe]], produced Car'n's kloo horn—in doing so defusing the situation and effectively paying off the "debts" of his friends.<ref name="The Kloo Horn Cantina Caper" />

==Personality and traits==
{{Quote|'Heart' suggests the warmth and kindness one reserves for friends, yet men like us cannot afford to ''have'' friends. I consider you a mutually beneficial associate by profession—if I consider you at all.|Djas Puhr, to Han Solo|<ref name="The Kloo Horn Cantina Caper" />}}
Exploiting his species' keen senses and quick reflexes,<ref name="Sakiyan">{{Databank|sakiyan|Sakiyan}}</ref> Djas Puhr was a skilled tracker—effortlessly retrieving Lirin D'avi's kloo horn from a [[The Scrapper|Scrapper]] for his friend Lirin Car'n. As a bounty hunter, Puhr considered himself a professional and carefully analyzed the situations he found himself in; when he wished to do so, he would even wager on the outcome, sometimes just to consider the philosophy behind it.<ref name="The Kloo Horn Cantina Caper" />

Though Puhr retained some sentimentality when remembering his [[homeworld]], he was generally reluctant to have close relationships with others, even his drinking partners at Chalmun's Cantina. He felt that, in his line of work, personal attachment was dangerous, if not impossible. Nevertheless, Puhr found the concept of friendship intriguing, and considered Han Solo's gwayo egg smuggling as a foolhardy but admirable and thoughtful gesture.<ref name="The Kloo Horn Cantina Caper" />

Despite his work on Tatooine, Puhr hated [[Jabba Desilijic Tiure]] with a passion and refused to take bounties from him, holding other hunters that did so, like Greedo, in contempt. He also disliked the Empire and likened the [[Imperial Navy]] to a "refuse fleet."<ref name="The Kloo Horn Cantina Caper" />

==Behind the scenes==
Djas Puhr first appeared in [[Star Wars: Episode IV A New Hope|''Star Wars'': Episode IV ''A New Hope'']].<ref name="ANH" /> The name Djas Puhr was first revealed in the now-[[Star Wars Legends]] [[Star Wars Customizable Card Game]].<ref name="CCG">{{CCG|set=Premiere Limited|cardname=Djas Puhr}}</ref> The character was known as "Coal Man" on set and made from a [[Rick Baker]] off-the-shelf mask called "Future Man" that he made in [[1973]] to sell at [[Wikipedia:Halloween|Halloween]].<ref name="Archeology">{{YouTube|video=ElyMaaAFLKU|text=The Star Wars Cantina PT. 2 &#124; Full Panel #indianacomicconvention #tomspinadesigns #starwarshistory|channel=@FanXComicConventions|name=FanX Comic Conventions|date=2025-05-03}}</ref>

